    "publisher": "Northern Whig (via the British Newspaper Archive)",
    "kind": "news",
    "check": "names, labels, votes and sitting-member asterisks read on the Northern Whig page image (BNA art. 88): '... J. P. Tomelty, 608 (all Nationalists); *D. Perry, 715; *J. Leonard, 663; *J. Kelly, 630 (all Lab.). Unsuccessful—W. M'Cracken, 534; J. Press, 560; J. M. Quinn, 534 (Unionists); E. Quinn, 476 (Labour).' The Belfast News-Letter (22 May 1958 p. 2) prints M'Cracken's vote as 634, which would put him above an elected candidate; all three papers say the three Unionists were defeated, so the Whig figure is used (gap-fill 6 Nov 2026).",
