  "note": "Triennial election of the Downpatrick Urban District Council, twelve members elected at large, polled Wednesday 21 May 1958. Labels are the group labels printed after each list. W. M'Cracken's vote: the Northern Whig (22 May 1958 p. 4) prints 534, the Belfast News-Letter (22 May 1958 p. 2) prints 634. 534 is used because 634 would place him above two members declared elected (J. P. Tomelty 608 and J. Kelly 630) in an at-large election, while all three papers (Whig, News-Letter, Frontier Sentinel 24 May 1958 p. 1) say the three Unionist candidates were defeated. The arithmetic cannot settle it: the Whig's 'Total poll 16,286' matches neither vote total (10,649 with 534; 10,749 with 634) and no majority or electorate is printed. The order of the unsuccessful list does not settle it either: the News-Letter lists M'Cracken 634, Press 560, Quinn 534 (descending), the Whig M'Cracken 534, Press 560, Quinn 534."
